-- title:
--   Base change of a morphism of projective Weierstrass models
-- statement:
--   Let $f : T \to T'$ be a homomorphism of commutative rings and let $W_1, W_2$ be Weierstrass curves over $T$. For a Weierstrass curve $W$ over a ring $R$, `projModelCR W.toProjective` denotes $\operatorname{Proj}$ of the quotient of $R[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ by the ideal generated by the homogeneous Weierstrass cubic of $W$, graded by the images of the homogeneous submodules, and `projModelStrCR` is its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$. Assume given a morphism $u$ from the model of $W_1$ to that of $W_2$ commuting with the two structure morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec} T$, and, for $i = 1,2$, a graded ring homomorphism $\varphi_i$ from the graded ring of $W_i$ to that of $W_i$ base changed along $f$, such that the irrelevant ideal of the target is contained in the image under $\varphi_i$ of the irrelevant ideal of the source (so that $\operatorname{Proj}$ of $\varphi_i$ is defined), and such that $\varphi_i$ sends the class of a constant $C\,a$ to the class of $C\,(f a)$ and the class of each $X_j$ to the class of $X_j$. Then there exists a morphism $u'$ between the base-changed models which commutes with the structure morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec} T'$, satisfies $\operatorname{Proj}(\varphi_2) \circ u' = u \circ \operatorname{Proj}(\varphi_1)$, makes that square cartesian, and is the unique morphism with those two commutation properties.
--
--   This is the base-change statement for morphisms of projective Weierstrass models along a ring map: a $T$-morphism of models descends to a unique $T'$-morphism of the base-changed models, and the resulting square is cartesian, so that properties stable under base change (finiteness, flatness, surjectivity, ranks) transfer to $u'$. It is used in the construction of the relevant $T'$-morphisms in `exists_hom_isFinite_flat_finrank_eq_of_map_map_eq_dualNumber`.
